F. Flintstone wrote:
> How can I make it so that a process can get more memory that it needs.
> I'm running a TSP program which requires 450MB but it never completes
> successfully and indicates that it could only aquire 130MB when it
> requested for 450MB. 

% limit datasize
datasize        131072 kbytes
(that's the default)

% limit datasize 500000

You may also have to adjust swap space settings so there is at
least this much swap space available.



