Check the directory /etc/fdmns,

there should be a directory for every domain and in that directory a
symlink pointing to /dev/vol/<domain_name>/<fileset_name>

So if your domnain is called usr_dom, your fileset usr, your diskgroup
rootdg and you volume usrvol, it would look like this:
/etc/fdmns/usr_dom/usrvol -> /dev/vol/rootdg/usrvol
this applies if you use LSM.

Also try running verify (instead of fsck!)

The message E_DOMAIN_NOT_ACTIVATED (see advfs_err(4)) means that the
domain has not been activated...
Check your diskgroup with volprint -htg <dg_name> for errors.

Hope this helps,

Cheers, Arndt


