For your first question, I think DEC came with a very good (i.e. optimized)
fortran compiler. Type "which f77" to see if you have it. If not, you can
consider installing GNU gcc/egcs which has a g77 frontend. Quite useful. 

http://sourceware.cygnus.com or http://egcs.cygnus.com

But if it is a commercial program that requires a fortran compiler, they might be
asking for f90, and I am not sure... it might require $$. do "which f90". 

For your 2nd question; your machine's new bahaviour is probably the correct one -
the old one is bad security-wise. For security reasons, root on many unices are
forbidden to get in directly from outside and the only place he can get on is 
in front of the computer itself (so that there is less possbility of password 
getting sniffed, etc). If you need temporary root privilege from outside, you can
log in as normal user and then "su root". "man su" for details. If you really
really want to allow root to login directly from outside (bad bad bad), you can
modify /etc/securetty or something like that. 

